CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ outer handler reached after rethrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ outer rethrow re-propagates the outer exception E\(1\): SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.throw]/8 -- a bare `throw;` re-propagates the exception the handler it
appears in is handling.  Fixed by keying the exception being handled per handler
(a rethrow lexically inside a handler is tagged with that handler's catch-var id,
and remove_cpp_exceptions gives each handler its own current-exception slot),
so a completed inner try/catch no longer clobbers the outer handler's exception.
